 {:db/id "q-94213/ma-source-field/32aa75919025d5e49b8544f7fed47bba91dd462c0d1fed75c0d214b4853b7c33" :answer-field/id #uuid "10ef20bf-2e5d-50b3-b950-69a099e3e7b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-94213/ma-source-field/32aa75919025d5e49b8544f7fed47bba91dd462c0d1fed75c0d214b4853b7c33/6e6afeb1c3697ad26c9b898ff0f8d7164de5bf4956b2226eb2896ba2a1d27ca4" "q-94213/ma-source-field/32aa75919025d5e49b8544f7fed47bba91dd462c0d1fed75c0d214b4853b7c33/7d851a04a9c3a163706062ceb71b3e6ac8be557a794587cfc0f7448494ac5176" "q-94213/ma-source-field/32aa75919025d5e49b8544f7fed47bba91dd462c0d1fed75c0d214b4853b7c33/2cf210ed394235943e42d6d7e2530352473fe02365ade484bdfbf16de1e3674a" "q-94213/ma-source-field/32aa75919025d5e49b8544f7fed47bba91dd462c0d1fed75c0d214b4853b7c33/a3a1323c01ddaec06865265ea57e361ae560a54e66eedb34274ab76b33e4945f" "q-94213/ma-source-field/32aa75919025d5e49b8544f7fed47bba91dd462c0d1fed75c0d214b4853b7c33/708894bea60481ac1c87a8e09b1ed8e951ad8b45b3b19165cefc19d3a3319e49"] :answer-field/correct "q-94213/ma-source-field/32aa75919025d5e49b8544f7fed47bba91dd462c0d1fed75c0d214b4853b7c33/2cf210ed394235943e42d6d7e2530352473fe02365ade484bdfbf16de1e3674a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-94213" :question/id #uuid "190daf82-0a4f-5d1d-bcce-07f33dc7233c" :question/math-academy-id "q-94213" :question/problem "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?" :question/worked-solution "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{3})+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}))+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})+({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2})+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-({x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-9{x}_{3}^{2}+14{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-7{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group ${x}_{2}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{2},$ factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{2}^{2},$ and complete the square inside the second parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2({x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3})-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2([{x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{3}^{2}]-4{x}_{3}^{2})-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2(({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2})-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+8{x}_{3}^{2}-7{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})^{2}-2({x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from top to bottom, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-94213/ma-source-field/32aa75919025d5e49b8544f7fed47bba91dd462c0d1fed75c0d214b4853b7c33"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
