 {:db/id "q-94278" :question/id #uuid "23f8b8a5-7c24-563a-a40e-d60abf329c96" :question/math-academy-id "q-94278" :question/problem "A particle is moving with simple harmonic motion. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5y=0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\nI. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+{ϕ}_{1})$\nII. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}t+{ϕ}_{2})$\nIII. $y=A\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\sqrt{5}t+B\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\sqrt{5}t$\n\nNote that $R,{ϕ}_{1},{ϕ}_{2},A$ and $B$ are constants." :question/worked-solution "The SHM equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=5\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{5}t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{5}t$\n\nTherefore, only statement II could be used to represent $y(t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94278/ma-source-field/a560ae60b6edc56c31acad3a619edfc6bdb230476dd31f4400a48b18eea7e67a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
 {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e17fe7fc-3b85-5f2c-aa69-2336b05b16b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-94304/ma-source-field/df8205593f0afbefdc35a91f0c6dc237305334e55acac0d9c55b838b51583b0e/eaac7a2a44d3917ee28944910c9a9c1afaab9b1d631707a5f84fc5b80149328c" :answer/id #uuid "cd83c873-17b3-53db-8554-5059d348276f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-94304/ma-source-field/df8205593f0afbefdc35a91f0c6dc237305334e55acac0d9c55b838b51583b0e/0cde7213d1e1ba3c98aefd0b0b3cd2806e45d0ed74e5b8251efd6e11b0b57d5b" :answer/id #uuid "25213c17-424a-52a3-9371-0722697b6bae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-94304/ma-source-field/df8205593f0afbefdc35a91f0c6dc237305334e55acac0d9c55b838b51583b0e/5229d35e6ea963bad83d7a13a9082603ad8608b16ddc393c8758eed7acf155fe" :answer/id #uuid "fe19165f-f1ce-59b5-81e9-0ecaae91fcfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=2\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}
