 {:db/id "q-94981/ma-source-field/6926d8985d67c894beee07b10ae71650aac9f6a0aaf5893496b64d308b88f701" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce3dc232-fc1d-50e4-99b4-15ed1b8fa187" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-94981/ma-source-field/6926d8985d67c894beee07b10ae71650aac9f6a0aaf5893496b64d308b88f701/9cf65d7612475443473406894e74c0b56d49466a3771cd3c8d689b69f6c73b36" "q-94981/ma-source-field/6926d8985d67c894beee07b10ae71650aac9f6a0aaf5893496b64d308b88f701/8ff0a87dad402c8bc52f23fb87590d490cc7b390a042722cd4fcb17e26b76b8e" "q-94981/ma-source-field/6926d8985d67c894beee07b10ae71650aac9f6a0aaf5893496b64d308b88f701/631cdda9ec94dd76eb67af68c308cfe93c4d599c4e511289e1c00b618352d6fc" "q-94981/ma-source-field/6926d8985d67c894beee07b10ae71650aac9f6a0aaf5893496b64d308b88f701/3c80913f3ce93159715d7df8a7849cb549d94e1f63450bde9a7f296d0060e4f8" "q-94981/ma-source-field/6926d8985d67c894beee07b10ae71650aac9f6a0aaf5893496b64d308b88f701/e36db1551111cecdb2585339e47f2c19f171f6928d92aec20dbcda0f54c1616b"] :answer-field/correct "q-94981/ma-source-field/6926d8985d67c894beee07b10ae71650aac9f6a0aaf5893496b64d308b88f701/631cdda9ec94dd76eb67af68c308cfe93c4d599c4e511289e1c00b618352d6fc" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "e9152817-159b-5a54-868d-fe52d19640cc"] :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ -4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4-\\lambda  \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )((4-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(20-4\\lambda -5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-16)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4)-4(4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4-4) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94981/ma-source-field/6926d8985d67c894beee07b10ae71650aac9f6a0aaf5893496b64d308b88f701"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
