 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "1a7c1d3e-ea07-5462-b92b-00ccbee66e53"] :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94982/ma-source-field/a5d9658b86628772b577305236e8dfb71c003a016b3688ba463ff7fc26994c8d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
