 {:db/id "q-95323/ma-source-field/e58fee4f8984d65506beaef19ff72ae6393e4517d100d602c5606cf9f0da0495" :answer-field/id #uuid "9eed5c36-5d57-5b08-a6c1-2725fe122f8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-95323/ma-source-field/e58fee4f8984d65506beaef19ff72ae6393e4517d100d602c5606cf9f0da0495/3136dc5eef671c527d15360859716983a1d63ade88c99695a4f259260b67a6ae" "q-95323/ma-source-field/e58fee4f8984d65506beaef19ff72ae6393e4517d100d602c5606cf9f0da0495/ca19c26ffde1877c79d66bf7da309be5025c0ec8c718d95953d8c5cfa14dcc54" "q-95323/ma-source-field/e58fee4f8984d65506beaef19ff72ae6393e4517d100d602c5606cf9f0da0495/56a29c933397a961dd3aa2f51f6b2b5793c1fbcee6397bea4bfb99dcf742b804" "q-95323/ma-source-field/e58fee4f8984d65506beaef19ff72ae6393e4517d100d602c5606cf9f0da0495/a1d3a0bfb4d700856d9fb14d1d861ba0bbc78f4b7d79ba9aec61a9bd1e355235" "q-95323/ma-source-field/e58fee4f8984d65506beaef19ff72ae6393e4517d100d602c5606cf9f0da0495/e4740eb48a5c28b07217afd6d265d9c05f0be91afa5ff3f1db20bcb637b24e8d"] :answer-field/correct "q-95323/ma-source-field/e58fee4f8984d65506beaef19ff72ae6393e4517d100d602c5606cf9f0da0495/3136dc5eef671c527d15360859716983a1d63ade88c99695a4f259260b67a6ae" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-95323" :question/id #uuid "5bd4cb7d-93c2-588f-99ae-34346d7bdefb" :question/math-academy-id "q-95323" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95323/ma-source-field/e58fee4f8984d65506beaef19ff72ae6393e4517d100d602c5606cf9f0da0495"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
