 {:db/id "q-95354" :question/id #uuid "ae342c4d-42b7-5fdb-833c-f679170c12f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95354" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1-\\lambda  & 0\\end{aligned}|+(1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ -(1-\\lambda )+(1-\\lambda )[(2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-1)] & =0 \\\\ -(1-\\lambda )+(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +1-1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95354/ma-source-field/cd7d92ddedcef9c88f4ffe075c0c793e7d4e3226f507e017fa8e0c5cc2bec17c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
