 {:db/id "q-95377/ma-source-field/8752db59339ca32f0b7e705b0514a6984eebdbadf10bdf2bcba394b763b614a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e48eb31-ad56-59b2-a6ab-bf3fcb90c449" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-95377/ma-source-field/8752db59339ca32f0b7e705b0514a6984eebdbadf10bdf2bcba394b763b614a8/b4d68991c50aa7a968ace58a5e3a02f7bc0fa21f1e6372ab0de9bfa1523b0ecd" "q-95377/ma-source-field/8752db59339ca32f0b7e705b0514a6984eebdbadf10bdf2bcba394b763b614a8/9a3baf1ea057ad53b26a9c6730cd4e163a910a71d41b998403d84ad5170b252d" "q-95377/ma-source-field/8752db59339ca32f0b7e705b0514a6984eebdbadf10bdf2bcba394b763b614a8/ae666ed08071dedb664fe813e43e3c2ebe500c1504f8e0d4e1a71544e12442f0" "q-95377/ma-source-field/8752db59339ca32f0b7e705b0514a6984eebdbadf10bdf2bcba394b763b614a8/529cb6fb054a82bd80836a0f37449bdefff25f3483d8f7d38d9f772b7053cecc" "q-95377/ma-source-field/8752db59339ca32f0b7e705b0514a6984eebdbadf10bdf2bcba394b763b614a8/0760200c171e1fb4383b27e69a5d34733d17fb780657db3f68d0d261c8bbce28"] :answer-field/correct "q-95377/ma-source-field/8752db59339ca32f0b7e705b0514a6984eebdbadf10bdf2bcba394b763b614a8/9a3baf1ea057ad53b26a9c6730cd4e163a910a71d41b998403d84ad5170b252d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-95377" :question/id #uuid "de321704-9fad-5ba9-910c-dac492b8f0a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95377" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )[(8-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-4)]+2(-2)(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4)+(-4)(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +4-4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95377/ma-source-field/8752db59339ca32f0b7e705b0514a6984eebdbadf10bdf2bcba394b763b614a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
