 {:db/id "q-95740/ma-source-field/f7f3c65436c3cfb434d7561ea019c02117fc218a0384d6e2e04b28335b1d83ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "cca16c8f-0c59-5841-b3a3-92dfe79e5561" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-95740/ma-source-field/f7f3c65436c3cfb434d7561ea019c02117fc218a0384d6e2e04b28335b1d83ad/ba449368af87cfa5b37b91162dc20a1ed9dfe75d16f871476ef073c405484567" "q-95740/ma-source-field/f7f3c65436c3cfb434d7561ea019c02117fc218a0384d6e2e04b28335b1d83ad/40ba95ed2451aa225b040939c37625bd576053341acbad682786b4d33425d91d" "q-95740/ma-source-field/f7f3c65436c3cfb434d7561ea019c02117fc218a0384d6e2e04b28335b1d83ad/9ba3cc1ed92563fdb44d16941719d869349e2538ed2a457ef7eea57bae2aaa56" "q-95740/ma-source-field/f7f3c65436c3cfb434d7561ea019c02117fc218a0384d6e2e04b28335b1d83ad/683fef70bb11a9d2eb7bd6652fca0d81a246f441c10661dbe10e9a0241e1f750" "q-95740/ma-source-field/f7f3c65436c3cfb434d7561ea019c02117fc218a0384d6e2e04b28335b1d83ad/de59d3d2da81efa0288600730167cc658cc68bc6e9ecdadcb3f7edbc1b278911"] :answer-field/correct "q-95740/ma-source-field/f7f3c65436c3cfb434d7561ea019c02117fc218a0384d6e2e04b28335b1d83ad/9ba3cc1ed92563fdb44d16941719d869349e2538ed2a457ef7eea57bae2aaa56" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-95740" :question/id #uuid "7137b58f-9c7e-5085-84ba-d76796abafd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95740" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $25{x}^{2}=(5x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{5}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{5}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{5}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡5x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95740/ma-source-field/f7f3c65436c3cfb434d7561ea019c02117fc218a0384d6e2e04b28335b1d83ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
