 {:db/id "q-95997" :question/id #uuid "faf8199f-ba88-5be4-8120-b99e0f1165ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-95997" :question/problem "What type of quadratic curve is defined by the following equation?\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the squares for the variable ${x}_{2}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2{({x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+2{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2{({x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2{({x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}, \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the pair of intersecting lines ${x}_{1}=\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95997/ma-source-field/64da75d65c80b8ca914b86805a89df6e1ff2d76d94c155ae0cfa94df468dd4ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
