 {:db/id "q-96437" :question/id #uuid "03a543d9-dbfd-5d8e-8e78-3838660e063d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96437" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-9I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-96437/ma-source-field/76541743e9e1d683d696c4566127f8fa8e36954cf8c04bf5fa70d3f0fefd7f64"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
